Word2Vec (Word to Vector) is an NLP technique that converts words into numerical vectors (arrays of numbers) so that a machine can understand 
the meaning and relationships between words.
Simple example
Instead of representing:
King
Queen
Man
Woman

as simple word counts, Word2Vec represents each word as a vector:
King  → [0.25, 0.71, -0.13, ...]
Queen → [0.28, 0.69, -0.10, ...]
Man   → [0.12, 0.45, -0.20, ...]
Woman → [0.15, 0.43, -0.18, ...]

The important point is that similar words get similar vector representations.

For example:
King ↔ Queen
Man  ↔ Woman

will have vectors that are closer to each other in the vector space.
Interview definition
Word2Vec is an NLP algorithm that represents words as dense numerical vectors based on their context, allowing machines to capture semantic relationships 
and similarities between words.

How it differs from TF-IDF
TF-IDF	Word2Vec
Represents words using importance scores	Represents words using dense vectors
Mainly based on word frequency	Based on surrounding context
Doesn't capture meaning very well	Captures semantic relationships
Sparse matrix	Dense vectors
Example: 0, 0, 0.45, 0, 1...	Example: [0.21, -0.45, 0.73...]


Key concept to remember:
TF-IDF → importance of a word
Word2Vec → meaning/relationship of a word
